    "curated_prompt": "QR code mode detection returns wrong mode for alphanumeric data\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen generating QR codes with alphanumeric data, the mode detection is returning the wrong encoding mode. Alphanumeric strings that should use MODE_ALPHA_NUM are incorrectly being assigned MODE_NUMBER.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\nfrom qrcode.util import MODE_ALPHA_NUM\n\nqr = qrcode.QRCode()\nqr.add_data('ABCDEFGHIJ1234567890', optimize=0)\n\nprint(f\"Expected mode: {MODE_ALPHA_NUM}\")\nprint(f\"Actual mode: {qr.data_list[0].mode}\")\n```\n\nThe string 'ABCDEFGHIJ1234567890' contains both letters and numbers, so it should be encoded using alphanumeric mode (MODE_ALPHA_NUM), but it's getting assigned numeric mode (MODE_NUMBER) instead.\n\nThis affects QR code generation efficiency since alphanumeric mode can encode this type of mixed data more compactly than treating it as 8-bit byte data.",
